From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Reed <reedswork@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 03:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Keep-alive PINGs only while a bidirectional stream is open

quinn's keep_alive_interval pings whenever the timer runs out, whatever
the connection carries, so a connection with nothing open would be kept
up for good. Chrome (quiche's QuicPingManager) pings a client connection
15 s after the last packet only while its session says to keep it alive
(QuicSession::ShouldKeepConnectionAlive: an active stream), and an idle
connection sends nothing until its idle timeout. Measured in headless
Chrome 157 against an HTTP/3 server: a request held open was pinged at
15, 30 and 45 s; with no request open there was no PING, and the
connection closed at its idle timeout.

The timer still runs out 15 s after the last packet received; the PING
goes only while a bidirectional stream, this side's or one the peer has
opened, is not yet over both ways (an HTTP/3 client's requests, a
WebTransport session's CONNECT stream). Unidirectional streams (HTTP/3's
control and QPACK streams, open for the connection's life) do not count.
---
diff --git a/src/connection/mod.rs b/src/connection/mod.rs
--- a/src/connection/mod.rs
+++ b/src/connection/mod.rs
@@ -1203,8 +1203,15 @@
                     self.kill(ConnectionError::TimedOut);
                 }
                 Timer::KeepAlive => {
-                    trace!("sending keep-alive");
-                    self.ping();
+                    // Only while a stream is open, as quiche: a client
+                    // pings when its session says to keep the connection
+                    // alive (QuicSession::ShouldKeepConnectionAlive, an
+                    // active stream), so an idle connection sends nothing
+                    // and reaches its idle timeout
+                    if self.streams.bidi_open() {
+                        trace!("sending keep-alive");
+                        self.ping();
+                    }
                 }
                 Timer::LossDetection => {
                     self.on_loss_detection_timeout(now);
diff --git a/src/connection/streams/state.rs b/src/connection/streams/state.rs
--- a/src/connection/streams/state.rs
+++ b/src/connection/streams/state.rs
@@ -952,6 +952,19 @@
         expanded
     }
 
+    /// Whether a bidirectional stream is open and not yet over both ways:
+    /// one this side opened (an HTTP/3 client's requests, a WebTransport
+    /// session's CONNECT stream and its streams), or one the peer opened.
+    /// The peer's are kept here before it opens them; those are not counted.
+    pub(crate) fn bidi_open(&self) -> bool {
+        let open = |id: &StreamId| {
+            id.dir() == Dir::Bi
+                && (id.initiator() == self.side
+                    || id.index() < self.next_remote[Dir::Bi as usize])
+        };
+        self.send.keys().any(open) || self.recv.keys().any(open)
+    }
+
     pub(super) fn insert(&mut self, remote: bool, id: StreamId) {
         let bi = id.dir() == Dir::Bi;
         // bidirectional OR (unidirectional AND NOT remote)
